- Honest PoST starts at 0. Honest slot j at j·r. Honest blocks X_j ~ Bern(α) with α=(1−a)p.
- d at t_A = max{j ≤ n : X_j=1} (0 if none), where n = floor(t_A/r).
- "online doesn't change and fresh does" = P(d ≥ F_slots). For F_slots finite: d ≥ F_slots iff honest produced ≥1 block in slots F_slots..n. If n < F_slots, impossible. P = E[1 − (1−α)^{max(0,n−F_slots+1)}].
- Fresh node always changes (given the adversary publishes). But wait: fresh node changes always — but publish happens at t_A regardless. So P(fresh changes)=1. The "partition" probability = P(online doesn't change AND fresh does) = P(d≥F_slots).
- If F_slots=∞, P=0 (online always changes since d<∞). Good.

