In e4_replica!, during an attempt, honest blocks arrive at rate 1−h=0.1, adversary at rate h=0.9. The deposit matures when sel reaches dep_b + Mdep. The adversary publishes when priv > sel. For Mdep=3, the honest needs 3 blocks; adversary needs to get ahead. With rate 0.9 vs 0.1, the adversary will mine many blocks quickly; but the publish condition is priv > sel. Starting priv=dep_b−1, sel=dep_b. The adversary needs priv ≥ sel+1 = dep_b+1, i.e., 2 private blocks. With rate 0.9, that's fast. So it should reorg almost always. But my result says cut 99.95% of the time. Let me check the code logic.

